@jghal Unfortunately, no. 

In the absurdity in #3303 that followed my "this might just be resolved" comment here, there might just be a workaround. Mentioned in #3303 is that some of the crashes are tied to a very specific _width of the tab text_. If you're hitting this super consistently, you might be able to set `tabTitle` to something other than "Windows Powershell" and have this go away magically.

The root cause of this issue is unfortunately still being investigated. #3394 made the "crash on drag to another monitor" far less prevalent, but there are still ways to repro this `E_LAYOUTCYCLE` that we're hoping to fix.

