I think part of the challenge reading this is using `std::pair<float,float>` for both a pair of sizes for the first and second child (as in `_CalcSnappedPaneDimensions`), then also as a pair of min/max sizes, as in this function. I think this could be substantially easier to read if you added a helper struct like so:
```c++
    struct SnapSizeBounds
    {
        float lower;
        float higher;
    };
```

To help identify the difference. For example, the code below would then be:
```c++
        return {
            std::max(firstSnapped.lower, secondSnapped.lower),
            std::min(firstSnapped.higher, secondSnapped.higher)
        };
```
Which would be certainly more readable.

